"""Single footer contract shared by Ads generation and final export."""

FOOTER_VERSION = "SPORTS CAVE BASELINE THREE-LINE FOOTER V1"
COMPACT_FOOTER_RULES = f'{FOOTER_VERSION}\nApply to every Sports Cave black footer in every ad format and staff account.\nKeep existing layouts that have no black footer; do not add a footer to them.\nRender exactly three lines: the existing dynamically selected HEADLINE, its exact assigned supporting line directly below it, and CLAIM YOUR EDITION.\nPreserve the headline wording, font, size, colours, gold highlights, underline, alignment and styling exactly. Do not rewrite, shorten or standardise headline variations, or move the supporting sentence into the headline.\nRestore the exact saved supporting sentence and historical selection rules; never invent replacement wording. Set it in Montserrat Regular, 24–26 px at 1024 px, softer warm off-white, centred on one line. Keep it secondary; no blank row or spacer.\nKeep CLAIM YOUR EDITION exactly unchanged, including its existing gold colour, typography, tracking and styling.\nKeep the full-width opaque matte-black panel flush to the bottom, with its one thin continuous restrained gold shimmer replacing the existing top separator in place; keep the footer height, background, typography and layout unchanged along the top. The footer background stays fully opaque with no fade, gradient, transparency or floating overlay. The top seam itself has a visible champagne-gold specular sheen varying softly along its length, with a restrained brighter section and gently fading luminous edges; never a uniform flat gold rule. Keep the shimmer thin inside the existing separator footprint, without an extra strip, increased footer height, lens flare or glitter.\nFor a square canvas, use approximately 18–20% footer height and 80–82% photograph. At 1024 px retain the existing 42–48 px headline and 26–28 px CTA, 64–72 px horizontal safe margins and at least 64 px bottom text clearance. Use compact clear inter-line gaps to balance the headline, supporting line and CTA within the same panel; never enlarge the footer to fit the restored line. Scale existing format typography and safe areas proportionally for other output sizes, fitting these three lines without excess black space.\nThe framed edition remains the dominant visual. Preserve all artwork, frame, room, brand-colour, realism and generation-workflow instructions. Restoring the supporting sentence must not add a scarcity claim or alter any product detail.\nUse the current OS-assigned three-line footer in every image call. Project image sources are visual references only; their missing wording or plain seam must not suppress the supporting sentence or shimmer. In the existing final creative review, inspect each actual cover for the exact headline, supporting/FOMO sentence, CLAIM YOUR EDITION and visible top metallic shimmer. Correct a missing line or flat separator through that review before final delivery, retaining the unchanged compact footer, branding and complete framed edition. No new approval, separate compositor or asset-pasting requirement. Report unresolved defects honestly.\n\nEXACT FOOTER TEXT AND LINE COUNT\nUse exactly three visible text baselines: line 1 = the assigned HEADLINE; line 2 = the assigned SUPPORTING LINE; line 3 = the assigned CTA. Each field occupies one centred line. These three fields are the complete footer text, not examples to embellish.\nApply gold colour and the fine underline only to digits already inside the assigned headline. Keep those digits on the headline baseline; never extract, repeat or retype the number as a separate caption, quantity label, badge or scarcity row. An underline is a non-text stroke and does not create another text baseline. The top shimmer is also a non-text seam.\nDo not append an additional scarcity phrase, stock label, product subtitle, slogan or microcopy. Preserve text printed inside the original framed edition; it is not footer copy and must not be erased or copied into the footer.\nDuring final creative review and JPEG export, read the actual footer from top to bottom and count visible text baselines. Compare each line verbatim with its assigned field. Any extra text, missing field or wrapped field requires correction in that existing review before delivery. Correct only the footer while retaining the approved room and complete framed edition. Inspect the exported JPEG again at full size and mobile size. Emit the completion marker only after that exported image has exactly these three lines; report an unresolved defect honestly instead of claiming verification.\n'


def apply_footer_contract(prompt):
    """Include the shared policy once at the public prompt boundary."""
    if COMPACT_FOOTER_RULES in prompt:
        return prompt
    return COMPACT_FOOTER_RULES + "\n\n" + prompt
